  "description": "Works to trees in a Conservation Area: T1 (Large Cherry tree) - Remove dead wood, reduce canopy back from building to give 2 m clearance. Lift canopy to 2.5 m. Reduce lower lateral limb to rest of canopy. \rT2 - Medium twin stem Cherry tree, included bark. Remove rear stem. \rRear of house 8. \rT3 - Reduce canopy of Norway maple which is almost touching the building to give 2m clearance.\rGrass area near rear exit\rT4 - Large Ash tree. Reduce canopy back from neighbours gardens to give 4m clearance. \rGrass area around perimeter with Grove Vale\rT5 - Large beech tree. Reduce canopy back from building to give 4m clearance. \rG1- 2 Medium Cherry trees. Crown thin canopies by 20%, reduce canopies back from building to give 2m clearance and lift to 2.5m.\rLarge central grass area \rT6 - Large cherry plum. Lift canopy to 2.5m and crown thin by 20% removing epicormic growth. \rT7 - Cherry plum next to childrens play area. Tree has significant die back in crown. Remove to ground level and grind stump. Replace with min. 10-12cm stem girth Prunus cerasifera.\rT8 - Large Sycamore tree. Reduce canopy back from building to give 3m clearance. \rT9 - Multi stem Hazel, lapsed coppice. Thin canopy by 20% by removing epicormic growth.",
